cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PhosphoRLIE in your research, please cite it as follows."
title: "Kinase MD 2.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Hu"
    given-names: "Xiaojiang"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Smallriver2024/phosphorlie-skill"
url: "https://github.com/Smallriver2024/phosphorlie-skill"
abstract: >-
  PhosphoRLIE is an LLM-based framework and Claude Code skill for structured
  extraction of post-translational modification (PTM) regulatory events from
  biomedical literature. It extracts kinase-substrate-disease-drug relationships
  from PubMed titles and abstracts into richly annotated JSON records with
  confidence scoring and quality control flags.
keywords:
  - post-translational modification
  - phosphorylation
  - literature mining
  - large language model
  - bioinformatics
  - text extraction
  - PubMed
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-05-11"
